## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design offline-capable telemetry at the edge with guaranteed delivery and strict tenancy isolation.

## Key Concepts

- Edge buffering, per-tenant isolation, idempotent writes
- Out-of-order handling and replay-safe semantics
- Pluggable sinks and backpressure-aware flushing
- Testing offline durability and cross-tenant isolation

## Code Example

```javascript
class EdgeBuffer {
  constructor() { this.store = new Map(); }
  add(event) {
    const key = `${event.tenant_id}:${event.seq}`;
    this.store.set(key, event);
  }
  flush(toSink) { /* dedupe by (tenant_id, seq) and send in order */ }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you implement exactly-once semantics across edge and cloud sinks?
- How do you test failure modes like prolonged offline periods and partial flushes?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests real-world concerns: consent governance, dynamic schema evolution, cross-region data lineage, residency, and auditable privacy controls.

## Key Concepts
- Per-tenant consent governance and field-level filtering
- Edge filtering and region-local routing
- Schema evolution via Avro + schema registry with versioning
- Tamper-evident, immutable audit logs for lineage
- DSAR testing, data portability, and deletion guarantees

## Code Example
```javascript
function filterFieldsByConsent(event, consentMap) {
  const allowed = consentMap[event.tenant_id] || [];
  const filtered = {};
  for (const k of Object.keys(event)) {
    if (allowed.includes(k)) filtered[k] = event[k];
  }
  return filtered;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How to handle consent updates mid-stream without data loss?
- What metrics validate data minimization and retention policy?

## Why This Is Asked
This question assesses practical OTCA telemetry design skills, combining privacy compliance, multi-tenancy, and real-time pipeline constraints in a live streaming context.

## Key Concepts Tested
- OTCA telemetry patterns for streaming services
- Per-tenant residency and data isolation
- PII redaction at ingestion point
- Regional Kafka architecture with S3 Parquet sinks
- Tenant/date partitioning strategies
- Quota enforcement and traffic sampling
- Retention policies and lifecycle management
- End-to-end latency measurement

## Code Example
```javascript
const crypto = require('crypto');

function redactPII(userId) {
  return crypto.createHash('sha256').update(userId).digest('hex');
}

function partitionKey(event) {
  return `${event.tenant_id}/${event.region}/${event.date}`;
}
```
